---
import BaseLayout from '@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import LegalDraftNote from '@/components/LegalDraftNote.astro';
import F from '@/components/F.astro';
const updated = 'November 21, 2026';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Terms of Use | Speed Agency Websites for Trade Businesses"
  description="The terms for using the Speed Agency website: no guarantees of results, intellectual property, limits of liability and governing law. Projects are separate."
>
  <section class="page-hero wrap" data-hero>
    <span class="label">Legal</span>
    <h1>Terms of use</h1>
    <p class="muted mt-4">Last updated {updated}</p>
    <LegalDraftNote />
  </section>
  <section class="section alt" style="padding-top:var(--s-7)">
    <div class="wrap prose" style="max-width:68ch">
      <h2>About these terms</h2>
      <p>These terms cover your use of speedagency.online, run by <F k="LEGAL_NAME" />, trading as Speed Agency. By using the site, you agree to them.</p>
      <p><strong>Project work is not covered here.</strong> If you hire me, the terms for your project are set out in the written scope you approve before work starts.</p>

      <h2>Using the site</h2>
      <p>You may use this site to learn about my services and get in touch. Please don't misuse it: no attempts to break or overload it, no automated scraping, and no spam through the forms.</p>

      <h2>No guarantees of results</h2>
      <p>
        The information on this site is general. I don't guarantee any particular result from a website or service,
        including search rankings, calls, leads, revenue or conversion rates. Prices shown are starting points; your
        fixed quote is the price that applies.
      </p>

      <h2>Concept projects</h2>
      <p>Projects labelled "Concept project — demonstration only" were built to show my approach. They are not client work, and any business names in them are fictional.</p>

      <h2>Intellectual property</h2>
      <p>The text, design and code of this site belong to Speed Agency unless stated otherwise. You may share links to it, but please don't copy it wholesale.</p>

      <h2>Limitation of liability</h2>
      <p>
        I provide this site "as is." To the extent the law allows, I'm not liable for any loss arising from your use of the
        site or reliance on its content. Nothing in these terms limits liability that can't be limited by law.
      </p>

      <h2>Governing law</h2>
      <p>These terms are governed by <F k="GOVERNING_LAW" />.</p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>Questions about these terms: <F k="CONTACT_EMAIL" />.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
